{
  "_comment": "Shared parity fixtures for the slug rules. BOTH suites read this file: tests/test_slug_parity.py runs the Python implementation (stripe_link/domain/slugs.py) and the JS mirror (dashboard/src/composables/slugs.js) over the same cases and asserts identical output. An algorithm cannot be shared across Python and JS the way composition_rules.json is shared, so the FIXTURES are shared instead. Add a case here when you change either implementation.",
